WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:00.990
Fake products.

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:01.950
Fake friends.

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:02.950
Fake news?

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.342
These are bad connotations.

00:00:04.342 --> 00:00:07.559
But, fake data, turns out it's not so bad.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:08.980
Let's break it down.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.887
This fake data-- or synthetic data --as it's properly called,

00:00:11.887 --> 00:00:15.149
is in fact artificial, but not to machine learning models.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:16.410
Imagine this.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:17.267
You have a business

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:20.289
and you want to improve your customer recommendation system.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.415
You have a small data set of purchases

00:00:22.415 --> 00:00:25.679
and want to better match each unique customer that you come across.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.139
To do this, you need more data.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.774
Hence, synthetic data.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.999
Created by machine learning models,

00:00:31.999 --> 00:00:36.659
it can be generated in large quantities based off a smaller dataset of real data.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.900
This makes it ideal when data is scarce-- like right here.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.513
It's also useful for data privacy,

00:00:42.513 --> 00:00:46.860
and can be created without the need to collect and store sensitive personal information.

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:50.430
This can create fairer, less biased datasets.

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:52.020
I like this guy's style.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.721
Overall, synthetic data is an important emerging tool

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:57.149
that you should be on the lookout for.

